==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|līden}}, from {{inh|de|goh|līdan}}, from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*līþan}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*līþaną}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|lijden}}, {{cog|en|lithe}}. The sense developed from “go, travel” via “endure” to “suffer”. This happened under the influence of {{der|de|gmh|leiden|t=to be sorry, suffer, be hated}}, from {{der|de|goh|leidēn}}, from {{der|de|gmw-pro|*laiþijan}}, and also the originally unrelated noun {{m|de|Leid|t=sorrow}}, which is cognate with {{cog|en|loath}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈlaɪ̯dən/|[ˈlaɪ̯dn̩]}}
* {{audio|de|De-leiden.ogg|audio}}
* {{audio|de|De-leiden2.ogg|audio}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb|leiden<litt,gelitten>}}

# {{lb|de|intransitive}} to [[suffer]], to experience [[pain]], [[sorrow]], etc.
#: {{ux|de|Lerne '''leiden''' ohne zu klagen.|Learn '''to suffer''' without complaining.}}
# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[suffer]], [[bear]], [[endure]], [[undergo]], [[experience]] (some hardship)
#: {{ux|de|Er '''litt''' höllische Qualen.|He '''suffered''' hellish torment.}}
# {{lb|de|intransitive|with {{m|de|an|t=from}}}} to [[suffer]] (from a disease or condition)
#: {{ux|de|Die Gefangenen '''leiden''' an Unterernährung.|The prisoners '''suffer''' from malnutrition.}}
#* {{quote-journal|1=de|date=April 20 2012|journal=w:Die Welt|url=http://epaper.apps.welt.de/welt/archiv|page=22|passage=Durch Passivrauchen steigt bei Kindern das Risiko, dass sie als Erwachsene an einer chronisch-obstruktiven Lungenerkrankung '''leiden'''.|t=By passive smoking, the risk increases in children that they suffer from chronic obstructive lung disease as adults.|accessdate=4 March 2020|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20130412065211/http://epaper.apps.welt.de/welt/archiv|archivedate=12 April 2013}}
# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[like]], [[tolerate]] (usually in negative contexts)
#: {{ux|de|Ich kann ihn einfach nicht '''leiden'''!|I just can't '''stand''' him!}}

